extends ../../_layout.pug

block vars
  - var root = "../../"
  - var title = "Manifesto – Black Milk Impulses released on Metarecords – Leo Auri"

block content
  article
    header
      h1
        a(href='index.html') Manifesto – Black Milk Impulses released on Metarecords
      time(pubdate) October 24, 2014
    p
      | Released by METARECORDS
      br
      | META 070
    p
      iframe(style='border: 0; width: 100%; height: calc(95vw + 217px); max-height: 1000px;' src='https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=278822084/size=large/bgcol=ffffff/linkcol=EE3D00/transparent=true/' seamless).

        <a href="http://blackmilkimpulses.bandcamp.com/album/manifesto">
        Manifesto by Black Milk Impulses</a>

    figure
      blockquote
        p.

          The music is presented as the accidental rumblings of a musical virus. The tracks tumble out of the speakers like an intoxicated businessman, but a close listen reveals that each piece is anything but inebriated…………..The joy of Manifesto is the sounds between the notes, sampled crowds, static and these interlude tracks of less than two minutes that contain the seeds of extended improvisations.

      figcaption
        a(href='http://tinyurl.com/AAJmanifestoCorroto' title='Mark Corroto for All About Jazz' target='_blank') Mark Corroto – All About Jazz
        br
    figure
      blockquote
        p.

          At any moment, any of the three players seems entirely free to do as they wish, whether that be to inject a melody, a solo or a burst of rhythm; by some alchemy, that does not lead to a free-for-all or a cacophony but music that is focused, coherent and fluid.

      figcaption
        a(href='http://tinyurl.com/AAJmanifestoEyles' title='John Eyles for All About Jazz' target='_blank') John Eyles – All About Jazz
        br
    aside
      h4 credits
      p released 24 October 2014
      p
        a(href='http://www.gerhardgschloessl.de/' title='Gerhard Gschlößl') Gerhard Gschlößl
        |  – Trombone
        br
        a(href='http://gianpaolocamplese.it/' title='Gianpaolo Camplese') Gianpaolo Camplese
        |  – Drums
        br
        | Leo Auri – Piano, Electronics
      p
        | Artwork: details from “Keizoku” by 
        a(href='http://karahogudiary.tumblr.com' title='the institute of tangle * untangles' target='_blank') tttttan
      p
        | Mixing Track 9 – 
        a(href='http://stustustudiolein.de/' title='STU STU STUDIOLEIN' target='_blank') Ramin Bijan
        br
        | Mastering – Lars Kirchbach
        br
  nav.
